VTID-03824 — commands.log
==========================

## Reproduce the report

User reported (screenshot of the Command Hub /admin/device-preview ORB
overlay attached to the task): says "okay du kannst jetzt ausschalten"
("okay, you can turn off now") to Vitana in an ORB voice session. Vitana
speaks a farewell acknowledging it ("...ich schalte jetzt aus...") but the
overlay then flips to LISTENING mode instead of closing.

## Investigate the pipeline (background Explore agent, then read directly)

Traced the full click-to-close pipeline across both repos:
- services/gateway/src/routes/orb-live.ts (executeLiveApiToolInner —
  server-side tool dispatch)
- services/gateway/src/orb/live/tools/live-tool-catalog.ts (tool
  declarations sent to the model)
- services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js (client — turn
  handling, orb_directive dispatch, overlay teardown)
- services/gateway/src/orb/live/instruction/live-system-instruction.ts
  (system prompt)

Found: two existing narrowly-scoped tools already do exactly this mechanic
for their own flows — `end_teaching_session` (orb-live.ts:6505,
live-tool-catalog.ts:2524) and `end_guided_topic_teaching`
(orb-live.ts:6545, live-tool-catalog.ts:2562) — but nothing exists for an
ordinary conversation. `orb-widget.js`'s `turn_complete` handler
(_waitForAudioEnd, ~line 2759) unconditionally re-arms the mic into
LISTENING once audio drains, UNLESS `_isClosingForNav()` (line ~4750)
returns true — which it only did for `navigationPending`/`signupClosing`,
never for a plain "the user is done talking".

$ grep -n "end_teaching_session\|end_guided_topic_teaching" services/gateway/src/routes/orb-live.ts
-> confirms the exact dispatch shape to mirror (orb_directive over
   SSE/WS, best-effort try/catch, session-level flag, emitDiag call).

$ grep -n "_isClosingForNav\|navigationPending = false" services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js
-> confirms the single generic escape hatch and the session-start /
   _hide() reset sites that must ALSO clear the new flag to avoid leaking
   state across sessions (the exact bug class VTID-03799's own host-
   callback wiring test and VTID-03763's stale-poll guard both exist to
   catch in this file).

## Implement

- live-tool-catalog.ts: new `end_conversation` tool declaration, same
  shape as the two sibling tools.
- orb-live.ts: new `case 'end_conversation':` dispatch handler, emits
  `{type:'orb_directive', directive:'end_conversation', reason, vtid:
  'VTID-03824'}` over SSE/WS.
- live-system-instruction.ts: new "ENDING THE CONVERSATION" block in
  GENERAL BEHAVIOR — an English-language INTENT instruction (NEVER-rule 41
  — no hardcoded spoken sentence), telling the model to speak its own
  brief farewell then call the tool.
- orb-widget.js: new `else if (msg.directive === 'end_conversation')`
  branch — sets `_s.conversationEnding = true` BEFORE polling for the
  farewell audio to drain (so `_isClosingForNav()` makes a racing
  turn_complete poll bail instead of a brief listening flash), waits for
  the audio to actually finish (not a fixed delay — a longer farewell
  isn't clipped), then calls `_hide()`. `_isClosingForNav()` extended to
  OR in the new flag. Flag reset in `_hide()` and at session start
  (mirrors `navigationPending`/`signupClosing`'s existing reset sites) so
  it cannot leak into a later session.
- init(opts): wires `opts.onConversationEnd` into `_cfg`, guarded on
  `typeof === 'function'` (the exact pattern VTID-03799's own host-
  callback diff test enforces for every `_cfg.onX` the widget reads).
- tool-manifest.json: catalog entry added for consistency with the two
  sibling tools.

